# R23 the summit of Rowan's Rise: the Wicker Man, the Crooked Man's end, Phillip in the ash, the road home. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ arrive
Narrator: A spiral of small stones crowns the hill, its stone-lined rays running out toward ten bonfires around the rim of scorched, rust-red earth.
Narrator: At its centre stands the Wicker Man, sixty feet of woven willow bound in wire and iron. Inside the cages of its chest and limbs, people are praying.
set wv_summit_seen
quest wickers_vigil shadow_of_the_wicker_man
-> END

~ effigy
Narrator: Through the willow ribs of the chest cage, you see a woman's calm face pressed in among villagers, goats, and sheep. One tear tracks down her cheek as she stares at nothing at all.
crooked_man [sly]: Look at her, my darlings! Ladies and gentlemen, the crowning piece! Not a tremble in her. Don't you just adore a bit of breeding?
-> effigy_menu

~ effigy_menu
* Call out to Adela -> adela
* Ask the Crooked Man why he does this -> why
* [if item:wv_barnaby_repellent and not flag.wv_repellent_used] Spray Barnaby's Wicker Man Repellent -> repellent
* Demand that he let them go -> demand
* Light the fire and end this -> begin
* Not yet -> END

~ adela
Narrator: Adela's eyes find yours through the woven bars. No spell, blade, or cry can reach her. She gives one small, polite shake of her head, like a lady declining a dance.
-> effigy_menu

~ why
crooked_man [sly]: Why? Because she is the offering, and I am the master of ceremonies! Because the Queen asked nicely, and I do love being asked. And because it will make a glorious fire.
-> effigy_menu

~ repellent
Narrator: You mist Barnaby's tonic across the lower weave. A sharp cloud of vinegar goes up, and the sixty feet of dry willow pay it no mind at all. A very long silence settles over the hill.
crooked_man [sly]: Oh, I like that one.
set wv_repellent_used
take wv_barnaby_repellent
-> effigy_menu

~ demand
crooked_man [angry]: Let them go? My dear, holding on is the one thing I have ever done well.
-> effigy_menu

~ begin
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice
Narrator: Fire takes the dry willow in a rush while masked dancers caper in the glare, the earth trembling under the stamp of their hymn.
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice_2
Narrator: Behind the blackening weave, you catch Adela's eye and a single tear before the sheet of flame takes her clean.
cutscene wv_final_sacrifice_3
Narrator: The burning giant lurches one heavy step forward, and both its hollow eyes catch fire.
cutscene end
set wv_wicker_lit
combat wv_wicker_man

~ crooked_end
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end
Narrator: The Wicker Man comes apart in a pillar of sparks that climbs past the moon, washing the whole hill in orange light for a breath.
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end_2
Narrator: Out of the drift of embers, something small, shrivelled, and crooked claws its way free, charred to the bone and still wearing its grin.
crooked_man [angry]: My Queen. My Queen! You promised me your right hand! I built your house, I kept your flock, I did every single thing you asked. Why have you...
cutscene wv_crooked_mans_end_3
Narrator: He falls still. Cold rain begins to hiss on the smoking ash.
cutscene end
set wv_crooked_end_seen
set crooked_man_destroyed
quest wickers_vigil the_ash
-> END

~ phillip_ash
cutscene wv_phillip_in_ash
Narrator: A man in a ruined evening coat stumbles up the rise, singed and out of breath, shouting the same name until he reaches the ash and stops dead.
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: Adela.
cutscene wv_phillip_in_ash_2
Narrator: He drops to his knees and puts both bare hands into the warm ash. When he lifts them out, a blackened necklace hangs from his fingers, its little planchette still whole.
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: She was waiting for me. She was waiting here the whole time, and I was in the wrong place.
cutscene end
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_menu
* Ask if he is badly hurt -> phillip_hurt
* Tell him she could not be saved -> phillip_saved
* Offer to help him bury her -> phillip_bury
* Leave him to his grief -> phillip_go

~ phillip_hurt
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: What difference does it make? The wisps led me up the wrong hill. I pitched into a stream. I don't know what I did, only where I wasn't.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_saved
phillip_druskenvald [sad]: I knew. I suppose I always did. Knowing doesn't make it any lighter to carry.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_bury
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: No. Thank you, truly, but no. I'll see to her myself. I ought to have seen to everything myself.
-> phillip_menu

~ phillip_go
Narrator: He folds the bones into the lining of his coat and walks back down the hill without another word, blind to the village, the dying fire, and you.
set wv_phillip_seen
-> END

~ rowan
Narrator: A flat stone at the spiral's centre bears a woman's name and an antlered hare. Village tales say Rowan climbed up to sit on the moon, though the scorched rock tells it plain: she was the first they burned here.
-> END

~ fall_back
Narrator: The track back down lies open. The village is far behind you, and those chained in the willow cages above have very little time left.
-> vigil/square:retreat_confirm

~ home
Narrator: You take the road down from the rise through a night that smells of wet ash. Behind you, the ten bonfires gutter out one by one under a moon that is still too big, and still grinning.
set wicker_man_burned
quest wickers_vigil ashes_to_ashes
xp milestone
move wickermoor_village
